guitar-gaps.w8.onnx — guitar note transcription (onset / offset / frame / velocity regression CRNN),
converted for in-browser inference. 10 s of 16 kHz mono audio in; four [1001 × 88] matrices out
(100 frames/s, MIDI 21–108). The log-mel front end is part of the graph.

Weights:        guitar-gaps.pth from https://huggingface.co/xavriley/midi-transcription-models
                (revision b7bec65a2b860aca72856b0feef58b5df407b777, SHA-256
                65483e7c0e340a90415b15b520687587698c8c728f5fa470a205f13ee45c6513) — Xavier Riley et al.,
                "GAPS: A Large and Diverse Classical Guitar Dataset and Benchmark Transcription Model"
                (ISMIR 2024, arXiv:2408.08653) and "High Resolution Guitar Transcription via Domain
                Adaptation" (ICASSP 2024, arXiv:2402.15258). License: MIT (model card).
Architecture:   Regress_onset_offset_frame_velocity_CRNN — Qiuqiang Kong et al., "High-resolution Piano
                Transcription with Pedals by Regressing Onset and Offset Times" (IEEE/ACM TASLP 2021,
                arXiv:2010.01815); code piano_transcription_inference (MIT), as forked at
                https://github.com/xavriley/piano_transcription_inference
                (commit 7568dc7f78b625e40cf9776e2806d164006610e3).
Conversion:     scripts/guitar_crnn_export.py — fp32 ONNX export (matches PyTorch to 1.8e-6), then
                weight-only int8 (per-channel scale + DequantizeLinear; activations stay fp32).
                GuitarSet note F1 (30 tracks): fp32 83.1 %, this file 83.3 %.

